{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PdNigq2w38dxPiiWvJMAnu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for the \"median\" tier across all planned experiments in the experiment_plan. Each prediction needs a `result_rationale` explaining why this result would occur at this tier level.\n\nLet me carefully review:\n\n1. The median tier definition gives specific metric ranges and narrative guidance\n2. I need to cover all planned experiments: exp-001, exp-001b, exp-002, exp-003, exp-004, exp-005, exp-006, exp-007, exp-008\n3. Some experiments already have actual data (exp-001 components are done) - but the plan still lists exp-001 as \"planned\" in the experiment_plan section. \n\nLooking at the registry, exp-001 is actually complete with four models tested, and the paper_framing already references this actual data. The experiment_plan entry appears to be the original plan while the registry shows what's been executed. So exp-001 is done, and I need to generate median-tier predictions for the remaining experiments: exp-001b through exp-008. them as requested. For the median tier interpretation, I'm establishing the key characteristics that define this performance level—gradients that exist but with noise, separability that holds on MMLU though with some ambiguity in other experiments, and specific ranges for the various metrics that reflect a middle-ground performance profile rather than the strongest or weakest outcomes.\n\nNow I'm drafting the YAML configuration for each experiment. For exp-001, I already have the actual empirical data locked in—4 models across multiple precision levels, prompts, seeds, temperatures, and orderings tested on 200 MMLU items, with concrete results showing item effects at 42.1%, model-by-item interactions at 33.6%, and a generalizability coefficient of 0.820. The median tier classification for this experiment is really about how the subsequent experiments compare to these established baselines. Moving into exp-001b, I need to specify how the design differs from the original.\n\nFor exp-001b, I'm examining sampling stability by running three independent 200-item samples to see if the item dominance finding holds up, expecting the coefficient of variation around 5-10% to show the effect is robust despite some natural variability. Exp-002 tests whether these patterns generalize across multiple benchmarks, where I anticipate item effects ranging from 8-14 percentage points depending on the benchmark, with GSM8K showing particularly wide ranges and at least one anomalous benchmark breaking the otherwise consistent gradient. Exp-003 explores hardware and methodology interactions, where I expect these factors to account for only 1-3% of variance, weakening separability somewhat but not fundamentally. Exp-004 serves as the comprehensive synthesis pulling together all the previous experiments' findings. Exp-005 investigates whether scaling to 14B models produces meaningful changes in the variance hierarchy, expecting modest effects. Exp-006 examines fine-tuning's impact on the variance structure, anticipating a different hierarchy emerges but the analysis cuts off before I finish that thought.\n\nI'm also planning to check LayerCast and the MATH benchmark as additional validation points.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16422,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16422},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecd9a1c2-6cfe-459e-a8ac-e63e308c50da","uuid":"7ff48993-f6aa-4238-a2c9-0e02c0872ff4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PdNigq2w38dxPiiWvJMAnu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Gradient存在但需要从\"monotonic task-type gradient\"降级为\"benchmark-conditional variance structure\"——\n  不再claim系统性趋势，改为描述各benchmark各自的variance profile。Primary contribution权重从gradient\n  转移到model×item quantification + D-study validation（这两个已经用MMLU数据锁定）。Separability claim\n  加scope qualifier：\"on the GPU architectures tested\"。IRT comparison仍成立但需要报告ratio的\n  benchmark-specific变异。去掉hook中\"across N benchmarks\"的强表述，改为\"benchmark-specific \n  reproducibility budgets reveal qualitatively different variance structures\"。一个anomalous \n  benchmark放appendix讨论。AAAI borderline accept (5.5-6.5/10)，需要writing质量和figure清晰度来补分。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full-scale MMLU precision study (4 models)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      4 models × 3 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items。\n      数据已采集完毕（345,600 records），此处为median档解读框架。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 345600\n      single_model_item_id_pct: 61.1\n      cross_model_item_id_pct: 42.1\n      cross_model_item_id_ci: [36.0, 48.8]\n      model_x_item_pct: 33.6\n      model_x_item_ci: [28.4, 37.9]\n      residual_pct: 19.5\n      G_item_4model: 0.820\n      G_item_ci: [0.782, 0.861]\n      d_study_3to4_delta: 0.004\n      bf16_vs_fp16_precision_effect: 0.0006\n      leave_one_model_out_G_spread: 0.023\n      per_model_interaction_mistral: 29.25\n      per_model_interaction_qwen: 27.11\n      per_model_interaction_gemma: 23.95\n      per_model_interaction_llama: 19.69\n      reml_vs_henderson_max_diff_pp: 0.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      这些是已锁定的实际数据，不受tier影响。exp-001是median档叙事的基石：\n      model×item=33.6%和D-study Δ=0.004是两个最强结果，不依赖cross-benchmark gradient即可独立成立。\n      Median档的关键在于exp-001的MMLU结果无法被exp-002干净地推广到其他benchmark——\n      但MMLU本身的故事（item difficulty is model-specific, D-study validated out-of-sample）\n      已足够支撑Contribution 1的核心论点。Leave-one-model-out spread=0.023说明4-model设计\n      在边界上稳定，但不如8-10 model设计那样robust，这在median档下需要在Discussion中明确讨论。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Single-model vs Cross-model Variance Decomposition (MMLU)\"\n        description: >\n          左列4个模型各自的single-model G-study（item_id ~58-64%），右列crossed 4-model设计。\n          关键对比：item_id从61%降到42%，model×item从0%升到34%。附REML确认列（Δ<0.5pp）。\n      - name: \"Table 2: Per-model Interaction Magnitude\"\n        description: >\n          4行×3列：model name, overall accuracy, model×item interaction %。\n          展示interaction与accuracy的负相关（Mistral最低accuracy→最高interaction）。\n      - name: \"Table 3: D-study Out-of-sample Validation\"\n        description: >\n          3-model predicted vs 4-model actual G_item，含所有4种leave-one-out组合。\n          Δ范围0.001-0.023，中位Δ=0.004。\n      - name: \"Table 4: BF16-vs-FP16 Sensitivity\"\n        description: >\n          With FP32 vs Without FP32的precision effect对比（0.4%→0.0006%），\n          证明FP32 anomaly是vLLM enforce_eager artifact。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: Stacked-bar chart — single-model vs cross-model variance decomposition。左bar: item_id=61%, residual=24%, 其他facets。右bar: item_id=42%, model×item=34%, residual=20%。视觉冲击：model×item从无到34%。\"\n      - \"Fig 2: D-study projection curve — G vs number of models (3→4→5→8→10→15→20)。标注G≥0.80 threshold在~4 models, G≥0.90在~10 models。4-model actual point与3-model prediction curve重合（Δ=0.004）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      MMLU数据是median档最坚实的部分。42%→34%的item_id→model×item分裂是清晰的、可复现的、\n      有理论基础的（不同模型的item difficulty profile不同是psychometrics的基本预期，\n      但33.6%的magnitude是新的经验发现）。D-study validation Δ=0.004是方法论上的强证据。\n      Median档的风险不在exp-001本身，而在exp-002能否将这个story扩展到MMLU之外。\n\n  - name: \"Item resampling stability test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001b\"\n    description: >\n      3个独立的200-item stratified sample（seeds 0, 7, 99）× Llama × 3 precisions × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 orderings。\n      测试item_id dominance是否稳定还是200-item sample的artifact。\n    expected_results:\n      sample_0_item_id_pct: 59.3\n      sample_7_item_id_pct: 63.8\n      sample_99_item_id_pct: 55.1\n      cv_item_id: 0.073\n      sample_0_G_binary: 0.345\n      sample_7_G_binary: 0.371\n      sample_99_G_binary: 0.328\n      cv_G_binary: 0.063\n      mean_item_id_pct: 59.4\n      sd_item_id_pct: 4.35\n      prompt_item_range_across_samples_pp: 1.2\n      seed_item_range_across_samples_pp: 0.8\n      cross_sample_item_difficulty_correlation: 0.71\n    result_rationale: >\n      CV(item_id)=7.3%落在median档的[5%, 10%]范围内。这意味着item_id dominance是real的\n      （3个独立sample都给出55-64%，远高于null的~0%），但具体magnitude有±4pp的sampling variability。\n      这不是artifact，但确实需要在paper中explicit讨论：报告的58-61% item_id有~7% CV，\n      读者不应over-interpret小数点后的精度。cross-sample item difficulty correlation=0.71\n      说明不同200-item sample间有reasonable consistency但不是near-perfect——\n      部分item的difficulty ranking在sample间shift，这与measurement theory一致\n      （200 items from 14K MMLU是~1.4%的sample，expected to vary）。\n      Median档下这个CV足够支持\"item dominance is robust finding\"但需要加caveat，\n      不能claim\"precisely 58.4%\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1: Item Resampling Stability\"\n        description: >\n          3 samples × 主要variance components (item_id, prompt×item, seed×item, residual)。\n          附CV行和mean±SD行。Highlight item_id的CV=7.3%。\n      - name: \"Table S2: Cross-sample Item Difficulty Correlation Matrix\"\n        description: >\n          3×3 correlation matrix of item p-values across samples。\n          对角线=1，off-diagonal=0.68-0.74，mean=0.71。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: 3个sample的variance decomposition stacked bars并排，展示qualitative stability（item_id都dominant）但quantitative variation。Error bars from bootstrap within each sample。\"\n    analysis: >\n      CV=7.3%是\"stable enough to report, needs explicit discussion\"的典型median档结果。\n      Paper中需要一段话说明item sampling variability，并argue 200 items from stratified sample\n      是reasonable compromise between computational cost和representativeness。\n      可以用D-study framing：即使item_id在55-64%之间vary，核心结论（item是最大variance source，\n      远大于precision/prompt/seed的main effects）在所有sample中都成立。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark replication (GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      4 models × 2 precisions (BF16/FP16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 2 temperatures × 4 orderings\n      在GSM8K、ARC-Challenge、HellaSwag各200 items上。测试cross-benchmark variance gradient。\n    expected_results:\n      # GSM8K\n      gsm8k_total_records: 230400\n      gsm8k_item_id_cross_model_pct: 32.5\n      gsm8k_model_x_item_pct: 38.7\n      gsm8k_prompt_x_item_pct: 8.2\n      gsm8k_residual_pct: 14.3\n      gsm8k_G_item: 0.743\n      gsm8k_separability_binary_pct: 0.3\n      gsm8k_d_study_delta_vs_mmlu: 0.018\n      gsm8k_irt_gtheory_ratio: 3.1\n      # ARC-Challenge\n      arc_total_records: 230400\n      arc_item_id_cross_model_pct: 39.8\n      arc_model_x_item_pct: 28.4\n      arc_prompt_x_item_pct: 6.1\n      arc_residual_pct: 18.9\n      arc_G_item: 0.768\n      arc_separability_binary_pct: 1.8\n      arc_d_study_delta_vs_mmlu: 0.026\n      arc_irt_gtheory_ratio: 4.7\n      # HellaSwag\n      hellaswag_total_records: 230400\n      hellaswag_item_id_cross_model_pct: 28.1\n      hellaswag_model_x_item_pct: 19.6\n      hellaswag_residual_pct: 31.8\n      hellaswag_prompt_x_item_pct: 11.2\n      hellaswag_G_item: 0.724\n      hellaswag_separability_binary_pct: 0.7\n      hellaswag_d_study_delta_vs_mmlu: 0.028\n      hellaswag_irt_gtheory_ratio: 2.8\n      # Cross-benchmark summary\n      item_id_range_across_benchmarks_pp: 13.7\n      item_id_ordering: \"MMLU(42.1) > ARC(39.8) > GSM8K(32.5) > HellaSwag(28.1)\"\n      gradient_monotonic: false\n      gradient_break_benchmark: \"ARC-Challenge\"\n      anomalous_benchmark: \"HellaSwag\"\n      anomalous_reason: \"residual dominates (31.8%), item_id + model×item together < 50%\"\n      cross_bench_G_item_min: 0.724\n      cross_bench_G_item_max: 0.820\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档的核心特征：gradient exists but not cleanly monotonic。\n      \n      GSM8K (math reasoning): item_id降到32.5%（vs MMLU 42.1%）因为math items的difficulty更依赖\n      model-specific reasoning能力——同一道algebra题对Qwen可能trivial但对Mistral impossible，\n      导致model×item=38.7%超过item_id成为最大source。这是\"task-type matters\"的最强证据，\n      但也意味着simple gradient narrative不成立——在GSM8K上model×item>item_id，打破了\n      \"item_id always dominates\"的pattern。G_item=0.743因为items在models间less generalizable。\n      IRT/G-theory ratio=3.1，低于MMLU的3.8，因为GSM8K的prompt sensitivity较低（math格式更固定）。\n      \n      ARC-Challenge: item_id=39.8%接近MMLU，但本应比MMLU低（science reasoning harder than knowledge）。\n      实际上ARC没有按expected gradient排列——它的item_id比GSM8K高，打破了\n      \"knowledge→science→math→commonsense\"的monotonic gradient。原因：ARC的4-choice format\n      与MMLU类似，format consistency导致item_id structure类似。但separability=1.8%是所有benchmark\n      中最高的（仍在median档的[0.5, 2.0]内），可能因为ARC的science reasoning对precision\n      有非trivial sensitivity。这是gradient non-monotonicity的关键anomaly。\n      \n      HellaSwag: 最anomalous——residual=31.8%占主导，item_id+model×item together < 50%。\n      原因：HellaSwag的commonsense completion format使得prompt variation的影响大于其他benchmark\n      （prompt×item=11.2%），而item difficulty对所有models都偏向easy or hard extremes\n      （ceiling/floor effect），压缩了item_id的range。这是median档要求放appendix讨论的\n      anomalous benchmark。HellaSwag作为anomaly其实enriches the story——\n      证明了\"no universal recipe\"的claim。\n      \n      Gradient总结：MMLU(42)→ARC(40)→GSM8K(33)→HellaSwag(28) 的item_id确实存在下降趋势\n      （range=13.7pp，在[8,14]内），但ARC和GSM8K的顺序与naive task-complexity prediction不符。\n      不能claim monotonic gradient，只能说\"benchmark-conditional variance structure\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Cross-benchmark Variance Decomposition (4 models, crossed design)\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × 主要variance components。每行一个benchmark，列为item_id, model, \n          model×item, prompt×item, seed×item, precision effects, residual。\n          Highlight: item_id从42%到28%的range，model×item从20%到39%，residual从15%到32%。\n          每个cell附bootstrap 95% CI。\n      - name: \"Table 6: Benchmark-specific D-study Budgets\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × items needed for G≥0.80/0.90。MMLU最efficient (~414 practical),\n          HellaSwag需要最多items (~680) 因为residual dominance。\n          附IRT comparison列（IRT recommended items）。\n      - name: \"Table 7: Cross-benchmark Separability Summary\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × precision×methodology interaction %。Binary scoring vs text scoring。\n          Range: 0.3-1.8% (binary), 1.2-4.8% (text)。ARC最高binary interaction。\n      - name: \"Table 8: IRT vs G-theory Ratio by Benchmark\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × IRT items / G-theory items / ratio。\n          Ratio range: 2.8-4.7×，exhibit benchmark-dependence。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: 4-benchmark stacked-bar variance decomposition并排。视觉上item_id bars从左到右缩短（MMLU→HellaSwag），但ARC打破monotonic pattern。HellaSwag的residual bar突出。Color coding统一。\"\n      - \"Fig 4: item_id% vs benchmark散点图，标注4个benchmarks。虚线连接不是monotonic——ARC在GSM8K上方。附error bars (bootstrap CI)。Caption讨论non-monotonicity。\"\n      - \"Fig S2: GSM8K model×item interaction heatmap (4 models × 200 items)。展示item difficulty ranking在models间的disagreement pattern。与MMLU的对应heatmap对比。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-002是median档的defining experiment。13.7pp range证明variance structure确实varies across \n      benchmarks，但non-monotonic pattern阻止了elegant gradient narrative。\n      \n      关键叙事调整：(1) 放弃\"systematic task-type gradient\"，改用\"benchmark-conditional variance \n      structure\"——4个benchmarks各有distinct variance profiles，不服从single ordering。\n      (2) HellaSwag的residual-dominance放appendix详细讨论（可能原因：item format特殊性，\n      completion-style vs MC-style）。(3) GSM8K的model×item>item_id是genuine finding——\n      在reasoning tasks上，哪些items难depends even more on which model，这strengthens \n      Claim 1的model×item story。(4) ARC的anomalous position需要讨论——\n      format similarity to MMLU可能override task-type effects。\n      \n      对paper结构的影响：cross-benchmark section从\"gradient across task types\"重写为\n      \"benchmark-specific reproducibility budgets reveal qualitatively different variance structures\"。\n      这更honest但less catchy。Writing quality需要compensate。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-hardware G-study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      4 models × 2+ GPU types × 2 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items。\n      测试hardware × methodology separability。\n    expected_results:\n      gpu_types_tested: 2\n      gpu_type_1: \"RTX PRO 6000 (Blackwell, 96GB)\"\n      gpu_type_2: \"A100 80GB (Ampere)\"\n      second_gpu_data_completeness: 0.65\n      hardware_main_effect_pct: 0.4\n      hardware_x_precision_pct: 0.6\n      hardware_x_prompt_pct: 0.2\n      hardware_x_temperature_pct: 0.3\n      hardware_x_methodology_aggregate_pct: 1.4\n      hardware_x_item_pct: 2.1\n      hardware_x_model_pct: 0.8\n      accuracy_delta_across_gpus_pp: 0.31\n      G_item_gpu1: 0.820\n      G_item_gpu2: 0.807\n      separability_holds: true\n      separability_qualified: true\n      data_incomplete_reason: \"second GPU scheduling constraints; 3 of 4 models completed\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义：exp-003 incomplete (only partial data from second GPU) OR \n      hardware×methodology = 1-3%。这里取\"partial data\"情景。\n      \n      Second GPU (A100) 只完成了3/4 models（Qwen run因scheduling conflict未完成），\n      导致crossed design不完整。可用数据的hardware×methodology aggregate=1.4%，\n      在median档的[0.8, 3.0]范围内——separability technically holds（<3%），\n      但不再是clean null result（MVP的<0.3%）。\n      \n      为什么1.4%而非<0.3%：不同GPU architectures (Blackwell vs Ampere) 的kernel implementations\n      不同，CUDA execution order的nondeterminism pattern不同。BF16的tensor core实现\n      在两代GPU间有微妙差异（Blackwell的TF32 tensor cores vs Ampere的），导致floating-point\n      rounding paths diverge more than same-GPU precision differences。这是genuine hardware effect，\n      不是confound——但magnitude仍small enough that separability \"approximately holds\"。\n      \n      hardware×item=2.1%更值得关注：某些items（特别是numerical reasoning items）在两个GPU上\n      给出不同答案，因为intermediate computation的rounding差异在boundary-case items上\n      tip the balance。这是item-conditional hardware effect——aggregate separability成立\n      但item-level不完全separable。\n      \n      Data incompleteness意味着：(1) 不能claim \"fully crossed multi-hardware\"；\n      (2) 3-model subset的variance decomposition有higher uncertainty；\n      (3) 需要scope qualifier \"on the GPU architectures tested, with partial crossing\"。\n      Paper中frame为\"preliminary multi-hardware evidence supporting separability\"而非definitive。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Hardware Crossing Variance Decomposition (MMLU, partial)\"\n        description: >\n          Single-GPU vs Two-GPU variance decomposition。新增hardware main effect (0.4%)，\n          hardware×precision (0.6%), hardware×methodology (1.4%), hardware×item (2.1%)。\n          标注: based on 3/4 models due to incomplete second-GPU runs。\n          CI widths wider than exp-001 due to reduced data。\n      - name: \"Table S3: Per-GPU Accuracy and G-coefficient Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          2 GPUs × overall accuracy, G_item, G_binary。Delta行: Δacc=0.31pp, ΔG=0.013。\n          3 available models的per-model breakdown。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S3: 双GPU variance decomposition对比（仅3 models subset）。Side-by-side stacked bars showing similar structure with hardware effects adding ~2% total。注明incomplete design。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-003的partial completion是median档的signature weakness。足够说\"separability approximately \n      holds\"（hardware effects < 3%），但不足以make definitive claims。\n      \n      Paper策略：(1) Claim 2 scope严格限定为\"numerical precision on tested architectures\"；\n      (2) hardware crossing results放secondary position，framed as \"preliminary evidence\"；\n      (3) 明确列为limitation: \"full hardware crossing remains for future work\"；\n      (4) 强调即使partial data，hardware×methodology的1.4%仍远小于item_id的42%和model×item的34%，\n      supporting the relative magnitude argument even if absolute separability is weakened。\n\n  - name: \"Comprehensive analysis package\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      对exp-001/001b/002/003数据的综合分析。包括model-as-facet, bootstrap CIs, D-study projections,\n      REML comparison, IRT comparison, power analysis, methodological defenses等17个分析子项。\n    expected_results:\n      # (a) Model-as-facet (already in exp-001 actuals)\n      model_as_facet_item_id: 42.1\n      model_as_facet_model_x_item: 33.6\n      # (b) Bootstrap CIs\n      bootstrap_resamples: 1000\n      ci_width_item_id_pp: 6.4\n      ci_width_model_x_item_pp: 4.8\n      ci_all_tables_complete: true\n      # (c) D-study projections\n      d_study_G80_items_practical_mmlu: 414\n      d_study_G80_items_all_random_mmlu: 510\n      d_study_G80_items_practical_gsm8k: 580\n      d_study_G80_items_practical_hellaswag: 685\n      d_study_G90_items_practical_mmlu: 1240\n      d_study_cross_bench_delta_range: [0.018, 0.028]\n      # (d) REML vs Henderson I\n      reml_henderson_max_diff_pp: 0.47\n      reml_confirms_henderson: true\n      # (e) Logprob scoring\n      logprob_item_id_pct: 54.2\n      logprob_model_x_item_pct: 28.1\n      logprob_G_binary_vs_logprob_delta: 0.08\n      # (f) Ranking stability\n      model_ranking_flips_across_conditions: 2\n      ranking_flip_models: \"Llama-Gemma at T=0.7/FP32\"\n      ranking_stability_kendall_tau: 0.87\n      # (g) Higher-order interactions\n      three_way_interactions_total_pct: 3.2\n      largest_three_way: \"precision×temperature×item = 1.1%\"\n      residual_after_higher_order: 16.3\n      # (h) IRT vs G-theory comparison\n      irt_recommended_items_mmlu: 116\n      gtheory_recommended_items_mmlu: 510\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_mmlu: 4.4\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_gsm8k: 3.1\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_arc: 4.7\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_hellaswag: 2.8\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_range: [2.8, 4.7]\n      irt_at_116_items_gtheory_G: 0.529\n      # (i) Power analysis\n      power_to_detect_3pct_interaction: 0.94\n      power_to_detect_1pct_interaction: 0.71\n      minimum_detectable_effect_at_80pct_power: 1.6\n      # (j) Practitioner guide\n      guide_sections: [\"budget_lookup_tables\", \"temperature_stratified_guide\", \"model_as_facet_template\"]\n      # (k) Fixed vs random sensitivity\n      fixed_facet_G_range: [0.611, 0.664]\n      fixed_vs_random_max_diff_pp: 5.3\n      # (l) Binary data analysis\n      bernoulli_obs_correlation: 0.83\n      bernoulli_ratio: 1.0008\n      null_simulation_item_id_pct: 0.08\n      obs_vs_null_ratio: 737.5\n      # (m) Bootstrap vs jackknife\n      bootstrap_jackknife_ci_width_ratio: 0.98\n      independence_violation_negligible: true\n      # (n) Design asymmetry sensitivity\n      mmlu_3x3_vs_2x2_item_id_diff_pp: 1.8\n      mmlu_3x3_vs_2x2_model_x_item_diff_pp: 1.1\n      design_asymmetry_robust: true\n      # (o) Full benchmark projection\n      G_at_14K_items_mmlu: 0.987\n      G_at_14K_text_metric: 0.043\n      # (p) Logprob across benchmarks\n      logprob_cross_bench_available: 3\n      logprob_cross_bench_note: \"HellaSwag logprob extraction requires format adaptation\"\n      # (q) GPU cost analysis\n      gpu_hours_for_G80_practical_mmlu: 18\n      gpu_hours_for_G80_practical_gsm8k: 31\n      gpu_cost_per_benchmark_usd: [45, 78, 52, 85]\n    result_rationale: >\n      exp-004是分析工作，不产生新数据，其结果质量由上游实验数据决定。Median档特征体现在：\n      \n      (1) IRT/G-theory ratio在benchmarks间varies 2.8-4.7×（median档的[2.5, 5.0]）。\n      MMLU的4.4×接近best档预期，但HellaSwag的2.8×拉低了range。HellaSwag ratio低是因为\n      其residual-dominance意味着G-theory和IRT都面临similar irreducible noise——\n      两者的差异主要来自prompt/seed/ordering facets，而HellaSwag的这些facets也不够separable。\n      这使得\"G-theory需要N×更多items\"的claim变成benchmark-dependent的，不能给single number。\n      \n      (2) D-study cross-benchmark delta在[0.018, 0.028]，在median档的[0.01, 0.03]内。\n      MMLU的D-study prediction极准（Δ=0.004），但GSM8K和HellaSwag的D-study projection\n      有更大uncertainty因为variance structure本身less stable。HellaSwag需要685 items for G≥0.80\n      （vs MMLU的414），因为residual dominance意味着更多items只能incrementally改善G。\n      \n      (3) Power analysis显示对3% interaction有94% power（足够），但对1% interaction只有71%——\n      这意味着exp-003的hardware×methodology=1.4%在统计上borderline detectable，\n      strengthening the \"approximately separable\"而非\"definitively separable\"的framing。\n      \n      (4) Fixed vs random sensitivity max diff=5.3pp（temperature as fixed vs random）。\n      不大，但也不negligible——需要在paper中报告both analyses，说明结论对facet classification\n      不敏感但exact numbers vary。这是median档的typical \"robust but not perfectly clean\"结果。\n      \n      (5) Logprob across benchmarks只完成3/4（HellaSwag需要format adaptation），\n      与exp-003的incompleteness呼应——median档的execution gaps。\n      \n      (6) Ranking stability Kendall tau=0.87说明model rankings mostly preserved across conditions，\n      但2 flips exist (Llama-Gemma at extreme conditions)——enough to say \"rankings are generally \n      stable\" but not \"perfectly stable\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: D-study Budget Table — All Benchmarks\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × target G (0.80, 0.90, 0.95) × items needed (practical config)。\n          MMLU最小(414/1240/2680), HellaSwag最大(685/1890/3950)。附IRT comparison列。\n      - name: \"Table 11: IRT vs G-theory Direct Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × IRT items × G-theory items × ratio × delta explanation。\n          Ratio range: 2.8-4.7。底部注释解释差异来源（prompt/seed/ordering facets）。\n      - name: \"Table 12: Power Analysis Summary\"\n        description: >\n          Interaction effect size (1%, 2%, 3%, 5%) × power at N=345,600 design。\n          Minimum detectable at 80% power: 1.6%。\n      - name: \"Table 13: Methodological Robustness Summary\"\n        description: >\n          8 robustness checks × result × pass/qualified/concern。\n          Most pass, fixed-vs-random和bootstrap-vs-jackknife are \"qualified pass\"。\n      - name: \"Table S4: Higher-order Interaction Decomposition\"\n        description: >\n          所有3-way及以上interactions。Total=3.2%，最大单项1.1%。\n          Residual从19.5%降到16.3%。\n      - name: \"Table S5: GPU Cost Projections for Recommended Budgets\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × GPU hours × estimated USD cost for achieving G≥0.80 design。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: IRT vs G-theory bar chart — 4 benchmarks, 每个有两根bars (IRT items, G-theory items)。Visual ratio从2.8×到4.7×。Annotation标注差异来自哪些facets。\"\n      - \"Fig S4: Temperature-stratified G heatmap — binary vs text × 3 temps × 4 benchmarks。Binary从0.76(T=0)到0.55(T=0.7)，text consistently <0.05。HellaSwag在所有temps都最低G。\"\n      - \"Fig S5: Fixed vs random facet sensitivity — bar chart showing variance decomposition under 4 different facet classification choices。Differences visible but < 5pp for main components。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-004的17个子分析在median档下大部分给出supportive但qualified的结果。没有任何分析\n      产生devastating finding，但也没有across-the-board clean results。IRT comparison是最强的\n      standalone contribution（ratio确实varies by benchmark但方向一致：G-theory always more \n      conservative），power analysis提供了needed methodological credibility。\n      \n      The practitioner toolkit deliverable is concrete: D-study budget tables + temperature guide + \n      model-as-facet template。这些不依赖gradient clean-ness，可以直接从benchmark-specific results生成。\n      \n      Logprob incompleteness (3/4 benchmarks) 对title \"Evaluation Metrics\"的支持weakened。\n      Median档建议修改title为\"...Across Benchmarks and Models\"或保留但在Discussion中\n      acknowledge logprob coverage不完整。\n\n  - name: \"14B model extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-14B和DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B在datacenter GPUs上BF16/FP16。\n      测试model scale对variance structure的影响。\n    expected_results:\n      models_completed: 2\n      qwen14b_accuracy: 0.761\n      deepseek14b_accuracy: 0.742\n      qwen14b_item_id_pct: 56.8\n      deepseek14b_item_id_pct: 52.3\n      combined_6model_item_id_pct: 39.1\n      combined_6model_model_x_item_pct: 36.8\n      combined_6model_G_item: 0.851\n      scale_effect_on_variance_structure: \"modest\"\n      precision_effect_14b_pct: 0.001\n      item_difficulty_correlation_8b_14b: 0.78\n    result_rationale: >\n      14B models在single-model analysis中显示slightly lower item_id（52-57% vs 8B的58-64%），\n      因为larger models在更多items上都答对（ceiling effect压缩item difficulty range），\n      同时在difficult items上的performance更variable（reasoning capability的variance更大）。\n      \n      Combined 6-model analysis（4×8B + 2×14B）中model×item增加到36.8%因为scale difference\n      引入了systematic pattern：14B models在hard items上disproportionately better，\n      创造了与item difficulty correlated的model×item interaction。G_item=0.851略高于\n      4-model的0.820，符合D-study预测（more models → higher G）。\n      \n      Precision effect在14B上更小（0.001%）因为larger models的representations更robust to \n      rounding，consistent with the \"precision matters less as models scale\" intuition。\n      \n      Item difficulty correlation 0.78 between 8B and 14B说明items的relative difficulty\n      mostly preserved across scales但not perfectly——some items are \"scale-sensitive\"\n      (easy for 14B, hard for 8B)。这enriches the model×item story但不改变qualitative conclusions。\n      \n      在median档下，14B results support但不dramatically extend 8B findings。\n      Contribution是confirmatory：variance structure qualitatively similar across scales。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S6: 8B vs 14B Variance Structure Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          Side-by-side: 4×8B-only crossed vs 6-model (4×8B + 2×14B) crossed vs 2×14B-only。\n          item_id, model×item, residual的对比。附bootstrap CIs。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S6: Item difficulty scatter plot — 8B mean p-value vs 14B mean p-value, per item。r=0.78, with items colored by MMLU subject。Scale-sensitive items (large residuals from regression line) annotated。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-005是P1实验，在median档下提供scale robustness evidence。不改变paper的core narrative\n      但回答\"does this hold beyond 7-9B?\"——answer is \"qualitatively yes, quantitatively \n      model×item increases slightly with scale diversity\"。放在Results的后半段或appendix。\n      如果AAAI页数紧张，可以summarize in one paragraph with full table in supplement。\n\n  - name: \"Fine-tuning G-study (RoBERTa)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      RoBERTa-large在SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA上fully crossed：6 seeds × 3 learning rates × 4 data shuffles \n      × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions = 432 runs/task × 4 tasks = 1,728 total runs。\n    expected_results:\n      total_runs: 1728\n      tasks_completed: 4\n      # SST-2\n      sst2_seed_variance_pct: 8.4\n      sst2_lr_variance_pct: 42.3\n      sst2_data_shuffle_pct: 5.1\n      sst2_gpu_pct: 0.3\n      sst2_precision_pct: 0.1\n      sst2_seed_x_lr_pct: 12.7\n      sst2_residual_pct: 18.6\n      sst2_G_coefficient: 0.72\n      # RTE (small dataset, high variance expected)\n      rte_seed_variance_pct: 18.9\n      rte_lr_variance_pct: 31.2\n      rte_data_shuffle_pct: 11.3\n      rte_seed_x_lr_pct: 15.8\n      rte_residual_pct: 14.2\n      rte_G_coefficient: 0.48\n      # COPA (very small, extreme variance expected)\n      copa_seed_variance_pct: 22.1\n      copa_lr_variance_pct: 25.6\n      copa_data_shuffle_pct: 14.8\n      copa_seed_x_lr_pct: 11.2\n      copa_residual_pct: 16.8\n      copa_G_coefficient: 0.39\n      # Summary\n      variance_hierarchy: \"learning_rate > seed×lr > seed > data_shuffle > residual >> gpu ≈ precision\"\n      inference_vs_finetuning_diff: \"item → learning_rate as dominant source; precision remains negligible\"\n      bui_comparison_note: \"RTE seed variance 18.9% consistent with Bui et al. (2025) RTES finding\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Fine-tuning variance structure qualitatively different from inference：learning_rate取代item\n      成为dominant source（42% on SST-2），因为fine-tuning performance对lr选择的sensitivity\n      远大于对individual evaluation items的sensitivity。seed×lr interaction（12-16%）显示\n      training instability是lr-conditional的——特定lr+seed组合触发divergence。\n      \n      小数据集（RTE: 277 examples, COPA: 400 examples）的variance极大。RTE的seed=18.9%\n      与Bui et al. (2025)的RTES=18.22 for RoBERTa on COPA高度一致，提供cross-study validation。\n      COPA的G=0.39说明在这个scale上fine-tuning evaluation根本不reliable without averaging \n      across many seeds×lr combinations。\n      \n      Infrastructure facets（GPU, precision）在fine-tuning中也negligible（<0.5% combined），\n      与inference results一致——这是separability claim的bonus evidence，\n      虽然来自不同setting (encoder-only fine-tuning vs decoder inference)。\n      \n      Median档下exp-006的结果是interpretable但需要heavy qualification：\n      (1) encoder-only RoBERTa ≠ decoder LLMs；(2) task scale (SST-2: 67K) ≠ MMLU scale；\n      (3) fine-tuning variance structure根本不同于inference（不是\"same hierarchy, different magnitude\"\n      而是\"different hierarchy\"）。作为Discussion section observation而非numbered contribution足够。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S7: Fine-tuning Variance Decomposition (4 tasks)\"\n        description: >\n          4 tasks × 主要variance sources (lr, seed, data_shuffle, gpu, precision, \n          seed×lr, residual)。附G coefficient per task。\n          Highlight variance hierarchy inversion vs inference。\n      - name: \"Table S8: Bui et al. (2025) Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          Our RTE/COPA seed variance vs Bui et al.'s reported values。\n          Show consistency despite different experimental designs。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S7: Inference vs Fine-tuning variance decomposition stacked bars side-by-side。Left: inference (item_id dominant), Right: fine-tuning (lr dominant)。Visual contrast of different variance hierarchies。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-006在median档下cleanly delivers its downgraded role：Discussion-section observation\n      showing fine-tuning has qualitatively different variance structure。不需要是primary finding。\n      Bui et al. alignment是nice validation。Publication-worthy as supplementary evidence\n      但correctly scoped as encoder-only preliminary result。\n\n  - name: \"LayerCast precision mitigation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      LayerCast (FP16 storage + FP32 compute) as additional precision condition on MMLU。\n      量化这种precision mitigation的variance reduction效果。\n    expected_results:\n      layercast_accuracy: 0.6821\n      layercast_vs_bf16_delta_pp: 0.07\n      layercast_vs_fp16_delta_pp: 0.05\n      layercast_item_id_pct: 60.8\n      layercast_precision_effect_when_included_pct: 0.0003\n      layercast_precision_x_item_when_included_pct: 0.02\n      variance_reduction_vs_3precision: \"precision effects collapse to <0.001% when LayerCast replaces FP32\"\n      G_binary_with_layercast: 0.614\n      compute_overhead_vs_fp16_pct: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      LayerCast本质上是FP16+FP32的hybrid——storage in FP16, compute in FP32。\n      其accuracy与BF16/FP16几乎identical（Δ<0.1pp），因为BF16≈FP16已经established (D005)，\n      而FP32 anomaly是vLLM artifact不是genuine precision benefit。LayerCast therefore不提供\n      meaningful accuracy improvement over BF16/FP16，但也不hurt。\n      \n      当LayerCast替代FP32加入variance decomposition时，precision effects进一步collapse——\n      从already-small的0.0006% (BF16 vs FP16) 到trivial的0.0003%。这是because LayerCast \n      produces outputs nearly identical to FP16。Precision×item interaction也negligible。\n      \n      在median档下这个结果是clean但不exciting——\"precision mitigation works but isn't needed \n      because precision effects are already negligible after removing FP32 confound\"。\n      12% compute overhead for no meaningful benefit。\n      \n      Paper价值：作为completeness/practitioner guidance——\"if concerned about precision, \n      LayerCast adds 12% compute cost for no detectable reliability improvement over BF16\"。\n      One paragraph in Results or appendix。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S9: LayerCast Precision Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          4 precision conditions (FP32, BF16, FP16, LayerCast) × accuracy, item_id%, \n          precision effect %, compute time。Shows LayerCast clusters with BF16/FP16,\n          FP32 is the outlier。\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      exp-007在任何档位都不是paper的关键实验。Median档下它提供了一个clean practitioner takeaway\n      但不影响任何core claim。如果AAAI页数紧张，可以完全放appendix或甚至cut。\n\n  - name: \"MATH benchmark extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      MATH benchmark (200 items) — 测试reasoning-heavy tasks where chain-of-thought \n      introduces additional variance的item dominance pattern。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 230400\n      math_item_id_cross_model_pct: 30.2\n      math_model_x_item_pct: 35.8\n      math_prompt_x_item_pct: 9.4\n      math_seed_x_item_pct: 7.2\n      math_residual_pct: 11.1\n      math_G_item: 0.731\n      math_separability_binary_pct: 0.4\n      math_irt_gtheory_ratio: 3.3\n      math_d_study_G80_items: 620\n      cot_variance_contribution: \"absorbed into prompt×item and residual\"\n      math_vs_gsm8k_correlation: 0.82\n      accuracy_range_across_models: [0.21, 0.48]\n    result_rationale: >\n      MATH是最hard的benchmark（accuracy 21-48%），item_id进一步降到30.2%（vs GSM8K的32.5%）\n      因为extreme difficulty items的Bernoulli variance更compressed (p near 0 → p(1-p) small)，\n      同时model×item=35.8%因为models在hard math上disagree even more dramatically。\n      \n      Chain-of-thought不是G-theory的显式facet——它被absorbed into prompt×item (9.4%) 和 \n      residual (11.1%) 中。不同prompts elicit不同CoT strategies，导致prompt×item比\n      knowledge benchmarks高。但residual=11.1%反而比其他benchmarks低——因为MATH items\n      are more deterministic once you fix model+prompt+seed (either the model can solve it or not,\n      less random guessing than MC formats)。\n      \n      G_item=0.731是所有benchmarks中最低的，因为item difficulty rankings在models间最不一致\n      (model×item>item_id)——达到G≥0.80需要620 items，最多。\n      \n      MATH与GSM8K的item difficulty correlation=0.82说明两个math benchmarks的difficulty structure\n      有substantial overlap——\"math reasoning\"作为一个category有internal consistency。\n      这partial支持了gradient narrative（math benchmarks cluster together），但仍不够\n      claim monotonic cross-benchmark gradient。\n      \n      在median档下MATH加入后5-benchmark picture变为：\n      MMLU(42) > ARC(40) > GSM8K(33) > MATH(30) > HellaSwag(28)\n      看起来更gradual但ARC的位置仍然anomalous（knowledge-like benchmark在reasoning-like位置）。\n      而且HellaSwag最低不是因为\"hardest reasoning\"而是因为format-specific residual dominance。\n      Gradient story remains \"qualitative, not monotonic\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S10: MATH Variance Decomposition\"\n        description: >\n          MATH的full variance decomposition，与exp-002的3个benchmarks format一致。\n          Highlight model×item > item_id inversion（与GSM8K类似pattern）。\n      - name: \"Table 5 (updated): 5-benchmark Cross-benchmark Summary\"\n        description: >\n          扩展Table 5到5 benchmarks。排序by item_id descending。\n          附gradient non-monotonicity注释。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3 (updated): 5-benchmark stacked bars。MATH插入在GSM8K和HellaSwag之间。ARC仍然anomalous。\"\n      - \"Fig S8: Math-specific analysis — item difficulty distribution (bimodal: many items near p=0 and p=0.4) explaining compressed item_id variance。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-008作为P2实验在median档下adds marginal value。MATH的结果与GSM8K qualitatively similar\n      （model×item > item_id），strengthening the \"reasoning tasks have different variance structure\"\n      observation但不解决gradient non-monotonicity。如果timeline紧张（AAAI 9 weeks），\n      这是第一个cut candidate——GSM8K alone已经demonstrate了reasoning-task variance shift。\n      \n      如果included，MATH的主要added value是(1) 5th benchmark for cross-benchmark comparison,\n      (2) lowest G_item showing hardest benchmarks need most items, (3) CoT variance analysis\n      showing prompt×item absorbs reasoning strategy variation。这些是appendix material。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16422,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16422},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecd9a1c2-6cfe-459e-a8ac-e63e308c50da","uuid":"3e3e0928-531c-4aa0-a2a9-2896d7e6863b"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":328379,"duration_api_ms":329808,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Gradient存在但需要从\"monotonic task-type gradient\"降级为\"benchmark-conditional variance structure\"——\n  不再claim系统性趋势，改为描述各benchmark各自的variance profile。Primary contribution权重从gradient\n  转移到model×item quantification + D-study validation（这两个已经用MMLU数据锁定）。Separability claim\n  加scope qualifier：\"on the GPU architectures tested\"。IRT comparison仍成立但需要报告ratio的\n  benchmark-specific变异。去掉hook中\"across N benchmarks\"的强表述，改为\"benchmark-specific \n  reproducibility budgets reveal qualitatively different variance structures\"。一个anomalous \n  benchmark放appendix讨论。AAAI borderline accept (5.5-6.5/10)，需要writing质量和figure清晰度来补分。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full-scale MMLU precision study (4 models)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      4 models × 3 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items。\n      数据已采集完毕（345,600 records），此处为median档解读框架。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 345600\n      single_model_item_id_pct: 61.1\n      cross_model_item_id_pct: 42.1\n      cross_model_item_id_ci: [36.0, 48.8]\n      model_x_item_pct: 33.6\n      model_x_item_ci: [28.4, 37.9]\n      residual_pct: 19.5\n      G_item_4model: 0.820\n      G_item_ci: [0.782, 0.861]\n      d_study_3to4_delta: 0.004\n      bf16_vs_fp16_precision_effect: 0.0006\n      leave_one_model_out_G_spread: 0.023\n      per_model_interaction_mistral: 29.25\n      per_model_interaction_qwen: 27.11\n      per_model_interaction_gemma: 23.95\n      per_model_interaction_llama: 19.69\n      reml_vs_henderson_max_diff_pp: 0.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      这些是已锁定的实际数据，不受tier影响。exp-001是median档叙事的基石：\n      model×item=33.6%和D-study Δ=0.004是两个最强结果，不依赖cross-benchmark gradient即可独立成立。\n      Median档的关键在于exp-001的MMLU结果无法被exp-002干净地推广到其他benchmark——\n      但MMLU本身的故事（item difficulty is model-specific, D-study validated out-of-sample）\n      已足够支撑Contribution 1的核心论点。Leave-one-model-out spread=0.023说明4-model设计\n      在边界上稳定，但不如8-10 model设计那样robust，这在median档下需要在Discussion中明确讨论。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Single-model vs Cross-model Variance Decomposition (MMLU)\"\n        description: >\n          左列4个模型各自的single-model G-study（item_id ~58-64%），右列crossed 4-model设计。\n          关键对比：item_id从61%降到42%，model×item从0%升到34%。附REML确认列（Δ<0.5pp）。\n      - name: \"Table 2: Per-model Interaction Magnitude\"\n        description: >\n          4行×3列：model name, overall accuracy, model×item interaction %。\n          展示interaction与accuracy的负相关（Mistral最低accuracy→最高interaction）。\n      - name: \"Table 3: D-study Out-of-sample Validation\"\n        description: >\n          3-model predicted vs 4-model actual G_item，含所有4种leave-one-out组合。\n          Δ范围0.001-0.023，中位Δ=0.004。\n      - name: \"Table 4: BF16-vs-FP16 Sensitivity\"\n        description: >\n          With FP32 vs Without FP32的precision effect对比（0.4%→0.0006%），\n          证明FP32 anomaly是vLLM enforce_eager artifact。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: Stacked-bar chart — single-model vs cross-model variance decomposition。左bar: item_id=61%, residual=24%, 其他facets。右bar: item_id=42%, model×item=34%, residual=20%。视觉冲击：model×item从无到34%。\"\n      - \"Fig 2: D-study projection curve — G vs number of models (3→4→5→8→10→15→20)。标注G≥0.80 threshold在~4 models, G≥0.90在~10 models。4-model actual point与3-model prediction curve重合（Δ=0.004）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      MMLU数据是median档最坚实的部分。42%→34%的item_id→model×item分裂是清晰的、可复现的、\n      有理论基础的（不同模型的item difficulty profile不同是psychometrics的基本预期，\n      但33.6%的magnitude是新的经验发现）。D-study validation Δ=0.004是方法论上的强证据。\n      Median档的风险不在exp-001本身，而在exp-002能否将这个story扩展到MMLU之外。\n\n  - name: \"Item resampling stability test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001b\"\n    description: >\n      3个独立的200-item stratified sample（seeds 0, 7, 99）× Llama × 3 precisions × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 orderings。\n      测试item_id dominance是否稳定还是200-item sample的artifact。\n    expected_results:\n      sample_0_item_id_pct: 59.3\n      sample_7_item_id_pct: 63.8\n      sample_99_item_id_pct: 55.1\n      cv_item_id: 0.073\n      sample_0_G_binary: 0.345\n      sample_7_G_binary: 0.371\n      sample_99_G_binary: 0.328\n      cv_G_binary: 0.063\n      mean_item_id_pct: 59.4\n      sd_item_id_pct: 4.35\n      prompt_item_range_across_samples_pp: 1.2\n      seed_item_range_across_samples_pp: 0.8\n      cross_sample_item_difficulty_correlation: 0.71\n    result_rationale: >\n      CV(item_id)=7.3%落在median档的[5%, 10%]范围内。这意味着item_id dominance是real的\n      （3个独立sample都给出55-64%，远高于null的~0%），但具体magnitude有±4pp的sampling variability。\n      这不是artifact，但确实需要在paper中explicit讨论：报告的58-61% item_id有~7% CV，\n      读者不应over-interpret小数点后的精度。cross-sample item difficulty correlation=0.71\n      说明不同200-item sample间有reasonable consistency但不是near-perfect——\n      部分item的difficulty ranking在sample间shift，这与measurement theory一致\n      （200 items from 14K MMLU是~1.4%的sample，expected to vary）。\n      Median档下这个CV足够支持\"item dominance is robust finding\"但需要加caveat，\n      不能claim\"precisely 58.4%\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1: Item Resampling Stability\"\n        description: >\n          3 samples × 主要variance components (item_id, prompt×item, seed×item, residual)。\n          附CV行和mean±SD行。Highlight item_id的CV=7.3%。\n      - name: \"Table S2: Cross-sample Item Difficulty Correlation Matrix\"\n        description: >\n          3×3 correlation matrix of item p-values across samples。\n          对角线=1，off-diagonal=0.68-0.74，mean=0.71。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: 3个sample的variance decomposition stacked bars并排，展示qualitative stability（item_id都dominant）但quantitative variation。Error bars from bootstrap within each sample。\"\n    analysis: >\n      CV=7.3%是\"stable enough to report, needs explicit discussion\"的典型median档结果。\n      Paper中需要一段话说明item sampling variability，并argue 200 items from stratified sample\n      是reasonable compromise between computational cost和representativeness。\n      可以用D-study framing：即使item_id在55-64%之间vary，核心结论（item是最大variance source，\n      远大于precision/prompt/seed的main effects）在所有sample中都成立。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark replication (GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      4 models × 2 precisions (BF16/FP16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 2 temperatures × 4 orderings\n      在GSM8K、ARC-Challenge、HellaSwag各200 items上。测试cross-benchmark variance gradient。\n    expected_results:\n      # GSM8K\n      gsm8k_total_records: 230400\n      gsm8k_item_id_cross_model_pct: 32.5\n      gsm8k_model_x_item_pct: 38.7\n      gsm8k_prompt_x_item_pct: 8.2\n      gsm8k_residual_pct: 14.3\n      gsm8k_G_item: 0.743\n      gsm8k_separability_binary_pct: 0.3\n      gsm8k_d_study_delta_vs_mmlu: 0.018\n      gsm8k_irt_gtheory_ratio: 3.1\n      # ARC-Challenge\n      arc_total_records: 230400\n      arc_item_id_cross_model_pct: 39.8\n      arc_model_x_item_pct: 28.4\n      arc_prompt_x_item_pct: 6.1\n      arc_residual_pct: 18.9\n      arc_G_item: 0.768\n      arc_separability_binary_pct: 1.8\n      arc_d_study_delta_vs_mmlu: 0.026\n      arc_irt_gtheory_ratio: 4.7\n      # HellaSwag\n      hellaswag_total_records: 230400\n      hellaswag_item_id_cross_model_pct: 28.1\n      hellaswag_model_x_item_pct: 19.6\n      hellaswag_residual_pct: 31.8\n      hellaswag_prompt_x_item_pct: 11.2\n      hellaswag_G_item: 0.724\n      hellaswag_separability_binary_pct: 0.7\n      hellaswag_d_study_delta_vs_mmlu: 0.028\n      hellaswag_irt_gtheory_ratio: 2.8\n      # Cross-benchmark summary\n      item_id_range_across_benchmarks_pp: 13.7\n      item_id_ordering: \"MMLU(42.1) > ARC(39.8) > GSM8K(32.5) > HellaSwag(28.1)\"\n      gradient_monotonic: false\n      gradient_break_benchmark: \"ARC-Challenge\"\n      anomalous_benchmark: \"HellaSwag\"\n      anomalous_reason: \"residual dominates (31.8%), item_id + model×item together < 50%\"\n      cross_bench_G_item_min: 0.724\n      cross_bench_G_item_max: 0.820\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档的核心特征：gradient exists but not cleanly monotonic。\n      \n      GSM8K (math reasoning): item_id降到32.5%（vs MMLU 42.1%）因为math items的difficulty更依赖\n      model-specific reasoning能力——同一道algebra题对Qwen可能trivial但对Mistral impossible，\n      导致model×item=38.7%超过item_id成为最大source。这是\"task-type matters\"的最强证据，\n      但也意味着simple gradient narrative不成立——在GSM8K上model×item>item_id，打破了\n      \"item_id always dominates\"的pattern。G_item=0.743因为items在models间less generalizable。\n      IRT/G-theory ratio=3.1，低于MMLU的3.8，因为GSM8K的prompt sensitivity较低（math格式更固定）。\n      \n      ARC-Challenge: item_id=39.8%接近MMLU，但本应比MMLU低（science reasoning harder than knowledge）。\n      实际上ARC没有按expected gradient排列——它的item_id比GSM8K高，打破了\n      \"knowledge→science→math→commonsense\"的monotonic gradient。原因：ARC的4-choice format\n      与MMLU类似，format consistency导致item_id structure类似。但separability=1.8%是所有benchmark\n      中最高的（仍在median档的[0.5, 2.0]内），可能因为ARC的science reasoning对precision\n      有非trivial sensitivity。这是gradient non-monotonicity的关键anomaly。\n      \n      HellaSwag: 最anomalous——residual=31.8%占主导，item_id+model×item together < 50%。\n      原因：HellaSwag的commonsense completion format使得prompt variation的影响大于其他benchmark\n      （prompt×item=11.2%），而item difficulty对所有models都偏向easy or hard extremes\n      （ceiling/floor effect），压缩了item_id的range。这是median档要求放appendix讨论的\n      anomalous benchmark。HellaSwag作为anomaly其实enriches the story——\n      证明了\"no universal recipe\"的claim。\n      \n      Gradient总结：MMLU(42)→ARC(40)→GSM8K(33)→HellaSwag(28) 的item_id确实存在下降趋势\n      （range=13.7pp，在[8,14]内），但ARC和GSM8K的顺序与naive task-complexity prediction不符。\n      不能claim monotonic gradient，只能说\"benchmark-conditional variance structure\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Cross-benchmark Variance Decomposition (4 models, crossed design)\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × 主要variance components。每行一个benchmark，列为item_id, model, \n          model×item, prompt×item, seed×item, precision effects, residual。\n          Highlight: item_id从42%到28%的range，model×item从20%到39%，residual从15%到32%。\n          每个cell附bootstrap 95% CI。\n      - name: \"Table 6: Benchmark-specific D-study Budgets\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × items needed for G≥0.80/0.90。MMLU最efficient (~414 practical),\n          HellaSwag需要最多items (~680) 因为residual dominance。\n          附IRT comparison列（IRT recommended items）。\n      - name: \"Table 7: Cross-benchmark Separability Summary\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × precision×methodology interaction %。Binary scoring vs text scoring。\n          Range: 0.3-1.8% (binary), 1.2-4.8% (text)。ARC最高binary interaction。\n      - name: \"Table 8: IRT vs G-theory Ratio by Benchmark\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × IRT items / G-theory items / ratio。\n          Ratio range: 2.8-4.7×，exhibit benchmark-dependence。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: 4-benchmark stacked-bar variance decomposition并排。视觉上item_id bars从左到右缩短（MMLU→HellaSwag），但ARC打破monotonic pattern。HellaSwag的residual bar突出。Color coding统一。\"\n      - \"Fig 4: item_id% vs benchmark散点图，标注4个benchmarks。虚线连接不是monotonic——ARC在GSM8K上方。附error bars (bootstrap CI)。Caption讨论non-monotonicity。\"\n      - \"Fig S2: GSM8K model×item interaction heatmap (4 models × 200 items)。展示item difficulty ranking在models间的disagreement pattern。与MMLU的对应heatmap对比。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-002是median档的defining experiment。13.7pp range证明variance structure确实varies across \n      benchmarks，但non-monotonic pattern阻止了elegant gradient narrative。\n      \n      关键叙事调整：(1) 放弃\"systematic task-type gradient\"，改用\"benchmark-conditional variance \n      structure\"——4个benchmarks各有distinct variance profiles，不服从single ordering。\n      (2) HellaSwag的residual-dominance放appendix详细讨论（可能原因：item format特殊性，\n      completion-style vs MC-style）。(3) GSM8K的model×item>item_id是genuine finding——\n      在reasoning tasks上，哪些items难depends even more on which model，这strengthens \n      Claim 1的model×item story。(4) ARC的anomalous position需要讨论——\n      format similarity to MMLU可能override task-type effects。\n      \n      对paper结构的影响：cross-benchmark section从\"gradient across task types\"重写为\n      \"benchmark-specific reproducibility budgets reveal qualitatively different variance structures\"。\n      这更honest但less catchy。Writing quality需要compensate。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-hardware G-study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      4 models × 2+ GPU types × 2 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items。\n      测试hardware × methodology separability。\n    expected_results:\n      gpu_types_tested: 2\n      gpu_type_1: \"RTX PRO 6000 (Blackwell, 96GB)\"\n      gpu_type_2: \"A100 80GB (Ampere)\"\n      second_gpu_data_completeness: 0.65\n      hardware_main_effect_pct: 0.4\n      hardware_x_precision_pct: 0.6\n      hardware_x_prompt_pct: 0.2\n      hardware_x_temperature_pct: 0.3\n      hardware_x_methodology_aggregate_pct: 1.4\n      hardware_x_item_pct: 2.1\n      hardware_x_model_pct: 0.8\n      accuracy_delta_across_gpus_pp: 0.31\n      G_item_gpu1: 0.820\n      G_item_gpu2: 0.807\n      separability_holds: true\n      separability_qualified: true\n      data_incomplete_reason: \"second GPU scheduling constraints; 3 of 4 models completed\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义：exp-003 incomplete (only partial data from second GPU) OR \n      hardware×methodology = 1-3%。这里取\"partial data\"情景。\n      \n      Second GPU (A100) 只完成了3/4 models（Qwen run因scheduling conflict未完成），\n      导致crossed design不完整。可用数据的hardware×methodology aggregate=1.4%，\n      在median档的[0.8, 3.0]范围内——separability technically holds（<3%），\n      但不再是clean null result（MVP的<0.3%）。\n      \n      为什么1.4%而非<0.3%：不同GPU architectures (Blackwell vs Ampere) 的kernel implementations\n      不同，CUDA execution order的nondeterminism pattern不同。BF16的tensor core实现\n      在两代GPU间有微妙差异（Blackwell的TF32 tensor cores vs Ampere的），导致floating-point\n      rounding paths diverge more than same-GPU precision differences。这是genuine hardware effect，\n      不是confound——但magnitude仍small enough that separability \"approximately holds\"。\n      \n      hardware×item=2.1%更值得关注：某些items（特别是numerical reasoning items）在两个GPU上\n      给出不同答案，因为intermediate computation的rounding差异在boundary-case items上\n      tip the balance。这是item-conditional hardware effect——aggregate separability成立\n      但item-level不完全separable。\n      \n      Data incompleteness意味着：(1) 不能claim \"fully crossed multi-hardware\"；\n      (2) 3-model subset的variance decomposition有higher uncertainty；\n      (3) 需要scope qualifier \"on the GPU architectures tested, with partial crossing\"。\n      Paper中frame为\"preliminary multi-hardware evidence supporting separability\"而非definitive。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Hardware Crossing Variance Decomposition (MMLU, partial)\"\n        description: >\n          Single-GPU vs Two-GPU variance decomposition。新增hardware main effect (0.4%)，\n          hardware×precision (0.6%), hardware×methodology (1.4%), hardware×item (2.1%)。\n          标注: based on 3/4 models due to incomplete second-GPU runs。\n          CI widths wider than exp-001 due to reduced data。\n      - name: \"Table S3: Per-GPU Accuracy and G-coefficient Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          2 GPUs × overall accuracy, G_item, G_binary。Delta行: Δacc=0.31pp, ΔG=0.013。\n          3 available models的per-model breakdown。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S3: 双GPU variance decomposition对比（仅3 models subset）。Side-by-side stacked bars showing similar structure with hardware effects adding ~2% total。注明incomplete design。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-003的partial completion是median档的signature weakness。足够说\"separability approximately \n      holds\"（hardware effects < 3%），但不足以make definitive claims。\n      \n      Paper策略：(1) Claim 2 scope严格限定为\"numerical precision on tested architectures\"；\n      (2) hardware crossing results放secondary position，framed as \"preliminary evidence\"；\n      (3) 明确列为limitation: \"full hardware crossing remains for future work\"；\n      (4) 强调即使partial data，hardware×methodology的1.4%仍远小于item_id的42%和model×item的34%，\n      supporting the relative magnitude argument even if absolute separability is weakened。\n\n  - name: \"Comprehensive analysis package\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      对exp-001/001b/002/003数据的综合分析。包括model-as-facet, bootstrap CIs, D-study projections,\n      REML comparison, IRT comparison, power analysis, methodological defenses等17个分析子项。\n    expected_results:\n      # (a) Model-as-facet (already in exp-001 actuals)\n      model_as_facet_item_id: 42.1\n      model_as_facet_model_x_item: 33.6\n      # (b) Bootstrap CIs\n      bootstrap_resamples: 1000\n      ci_width_item_id_pp: 6.4\n      ci_width_model_x_item_pp: 4.8\n      ci_all_tables_complete: true\n      # (c) D-study projections\n      d_study_G80_items_practical_mmlu: 414\n      d_study_G80_items_all_random_mmlu: 510\n      d_study_G80_items_practical_gsm8k: 580\n      d_study_G80_items_practical_hellaswag: 685\n      d_study_G90_items_practical_mmlu: 1240\n      d_study_cross_bench_delta_range: [0.018, 0.028]\n      # (d) REML vs Henderson I\n      reml_henderson_max_diff_pp: 0.47\n      reml_confirms_henderson: true\n      # (e) Logprob scoring\n      logprob_item_id_pct: 54.2\n      logprob_model_x_item_pct: 28.1\n      logprob_G_binary_vs_logprob_delta: 0.08\n      # (f) Ranking stability\n      model_ranking_flips_across_conditions: 2\n      ranking_flip_models: \"Llama-Gemma at T=0.7/FP32\"\n      ranking_stability_kendall_tau: 0.87\n      # (g) Higher-order interactions\n      three_way_interactions_total_pct: 3.2\n      largest_three_way: \"precision×temperature×item = 1.1%\"\n      residual_after_higher_order: 16.3\n      # (h) IRT vs G-theory comparison\n      irt_recommended_items_mmlu: 116\n      gtheory_recommended_items_mmlu: 510\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_mmlu: 4.4\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_gsm8k: 3.1\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_arc: 4.7\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_hellaswag: 2.8\n      irt_gtheory_ratio_range: [2.8, 4.7]\n      irt_at_116_items_gtheory_G: 0.529\n      # (i) Power analysis\n      power_to_detect_3pct_interaction: 0.94\n      power_to_detect_1pct_interaction: 0.71\n      minimum_detectable_effect_at_80pct_power: 1.6\n      # (j) Practitioner guide\n      guide_sections: [\"budget_lookup_tables\", \"temperature_stratified_guide\", \"model_as_facet_template\"]\n      # (k) Fixed vs random sensitivity\n      fixed_facet_G_range: [0.611, 0.664]\n      fixed_vs_random_max_diff_pp: 5.3\n      # (l) Binary data analysis\n      bernoulli_obs_correlation: 0.83\n      bernoulli_ratio: 1.0008\n      null_simulation_item_id_pct: 0.08\n      obs_vs_null_ratio: 737.5\n      # (m) Bootstrap vs jackknife\n      bootstrap_jackknife_ci_width_ratio: 0.98\n      independence_violation_negligible: true\n      # (n) Design asymmetry sensitivity\n      mmlu_3x3_vs_2x2_item_id_diff_pp: 1.8\n      mmlu_3x3_vs_2x2_model_x_item_diff_pp: 1.1\n      design_asymmetry_robust: true\n      # (o) Full benchmark projection\n      G_at_14K_items_mmlu: 0.987\n      G_at_14K_text_metric: 0.043\n      # (p) Logprob across benchmarks\n      logprob_cross_bench_available: 3\n      logprob_cross_bench_note: \"HellaSwag logprob extraction requires format adaptation\"\n      # (q) GPU cost analysis\n      gpu_hours_for_G80_practical_mmlu: 18\n      gpu_hours_for_G80_practical_gsm8k: 31\n      gpu_cost_per_benchmark_usd: [45, 78, 52, 85]\n    result_rationale: >\n      exp-004是分析工作，不产生新数据，其结果质量由上游实验数据决定。Median档特征体现在：\n      \n      (1) IRT/G-theory ratio在benchmarks间varies 2.8-4.7×（median档的[2.5, 5.0]）。\n      MMLU的4.4×接近best档预期，但HellaSwag的2.8×拉低了range。HellaSwag ratio低是因为\n      其residual-dominance意味着G-theory和IRT都面临similar irreducible noise——\n      两者的差异主要来自prompt/seed/ordering facets，而HellaSwag的这些facets也不够separable。\n      这使得\"G-theory需要N×更多items\"的claim变成benchmark-dependent的，不能给single number。\n      \n      (2) D-study cross-benchmark delta在[0.018, 0.028]，在median档的[0.01, 0.03]内。\n      MMLU的D-study prediction极准（Δ=0.004），但GSM8K和HellaSwag的D-study projection\n      有更大uncertainty因为variance structure本身less stable。HellaSwag需要685 items for G≥0.80\n      （vs MMLU的414），因为residual dominance意味着更多items只能incrementally改善G。\n      \n      (3) Power analysis显示对3% interaction有94% power（足够），但对1% interaction只有71%——\n      这意味着exp-003的hardware×methodology=1.4%在统计上borderline detectable，\n      strengthening the \"approximately separable\"而非\"definitively separable\"的framing。\n      \n      (4) Fixed vs random sensitivity max diff=5.3pp（temperature as fixed vs random）。\n      不大，但也不negligible——需要在paper中报告both analyses，说明结论对facet classification\n      不敏感但exact numbers vary。这是median档的typical \"robust but not perfectly clean\"结果。\n      \n      (5) Logprob across benchmarks只完成3/4（HellaSwag需要format adaptation），\n      与exp-003的incompleteness呼应——median档的execution gaps。\n      \n      (6) Ranking stability Kendall tau=0.87说明model rankings mostly preserved across conditions，\n      但2 flips exist (Llama-Gemma at extreme conditions)——enough to say \"rankings are generally \n      stable\" but not \"perfectly stable\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: D-study Budget Table — All Benchmarks\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × target G (0.80, 0.90, 0.95) × items needed (practical config)。\n          MMLU最小(414/1240/2680), HellaSwag最大(685/1890/3950)。附IRT comparison列。\n      - name: \"Table 11: IRT vs G-theory Direct Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × IRT items × G-theory items × ratio × delta explanation。\n          Ratio range: 2.8-4.7。底部注释解释差异来源（prompt/seed/ordering facets）。\n      - name: \"Table 12: Power Analysis Summary\"\n        description: >\n          Interaction effect size (1%, 2%, 3%, 5%) × power at N=345,600 design。\n          Minimum detectable at 80% power: 1.6%。\n      - name: \"Table 13: Methodological Robustness Summary\"\n        description: >\n          8 robustness checks × result × pass/qualified/concern。\n          Most pass, fixed-vs-random和bootstrap-vs-jackknife are \"qualified pass\"。\n      - name: \"Table S4: Higher-order Interaction Decomposition\"\n        description: >\n          所有3-way及以上interactions。Total=3.2%，最大单项1.1%。\n          Residual从19.5%降到16.3%。\n      - name: \"Table S5: GPU Cost Projections for Recommended Budgets\"\n        description: >\n          4 benchmarks × GPU hours × estimated USD cost for achieving G≥0.80 design。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: IRT vs G-theory bar chart — 4 benchmarks, 每个有两根bars (IRT items, G-theory items)。Visual ratio从2.8×到4.7×。Annotation标注差异来自哪些facets。\"\n      - \"Fig S4: Temperature-stratified G heatmap — binary vs text × 3 temps × 4 benchmarks。Binary从0.76(T=0)到0.55(T=0.7)，text consistently <0.05。HellaSwag在所有temps都最低G。\"\n      - \"Fig S5: Fixed vs random facet sensitivity — bar chart showing variance decomposition under 4 different facet classification choices。Differences visible but < 5pp for main components。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-004的17个子分析在median档下大部分给出supportive但qualified的结果。没有任何分析\n      产生devastating finding，但也没有across-the-board clean results。IRT comparison是最强的\n      standalone contribution（ratio确实varies by benchmark但方向一致：G-theory always more \n      conservative），power analysis提供了needed methodological credibility。\n      \n      The practitioner toolkit deliverable is concrete: D-study budget tables + temperature guide + \n      model-as-facet template。这些不依赖gradient clean-ness，可以直接从benchmark-specific results生成。\n      \n      Logprob incompleteness (3/4 benchmarks) 对title \"Evaluation Metrics\"的支持weakened。\n      Median档建议修改title为\"...Across Benchmarks and Models\"或保留但在Discussion中\n      acknowledge logprob coverage不完整。\n\n  - name: \"14B model extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-14B和DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B在datacenter GPUs上BF16/FP16。\n      测试model scale对variance structure的影响。\n    expected_results:\n      models_completed: 2\n      qwen14b_accuracy: 0.761\n      deepseek14b_accuracy: 0.742\n      qwen14b_item_id_pct: 56.8\n      deepseek14b_item_id_pct: 52.3\n      combined_6model_item_id_pct: 39.1\n      combined_6model_model_x_item_pct: 36.8\n      combined_6model_G_item: 0.851\n      scale_effect_on_variance_structure: \"modest\"\n      precision_effect_14b_pct: 0.001\n      item_difficulty_correlation_8b_14b: 0.78\n    result_rationale: >\n      14B models在single-model analysis中显示slightly lower item_id（52-57% vs 8B的58-64%），\n      因为larger models在更多items上都答对（ceiling effect压缩item difficulty range），\n      同时在difficult items上的performance更variable（reasoning capability的variance更大）。\n      \n      Combined 6-model analysis（4×8B + 2×14B）中model×item增加到36.8%因为scale difference\n      引入了systematic pattern：14B models在hard items上disproportionately better，\n      创造了与item difficulty correlated的model×item interaction。G_item=0.851略高于\n      4-model的0.820，符合D-study预测（more models → higher G）。\n      \n      Precision effect在14B上更小（0.001%）因为larger models的representations更robust to \n      rounding，consistent with the \"precision matters less as models scale\" intuition。\n      \n      Item difficulty correlation 0.78 between 8B and 14B说明items的relative difficulty\n      mostly preserved across scales但not perfectly——some items are \"scale-sensitive\"\n      (easy for 14B, hard for 8B)。这enriches the model×item story但不改变qualitative conclusions。\n      \n      在median档下，14B results support但不dramatically extend 8B findings。\n      Contribution是confirmatory：variance structure qualitatively similar across scales。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S6: 8B vs 14B Variance Structure Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          Side-by-side: 4×8B-only crossed vs 6-model (4×8B + 2×14B) crossed vs 2×14B-only。\n          item_id, model×item, residual的对比。附bootstrap CIs。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S6: Item difficulty scatter plot — 8B mean p-value vs 14B mean p-value, per item。r=0.78, with items colored by MMLU subject。Scale-sensitive items (large residuals from regression line) annotated。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-005是P1实验，在median档下提供scale robustness evidence。不改变paper的core narrative\n      但回答\"does this hold beyond 7-9B?\"——answer is \"qualitatively yes, quantitatively \n      model×item increases slightly with scale diversity\"。放在Results的后半段或appendix。\n      如果AAAI页数紧张，可以summarize in one paragraph with full table in supplement。\n\n  - name: \"Fine-tuning G-study (RoBERTa)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      RoBERTa-large在SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA上fully crossed：6 seeds × 3 learning rates × 4 data shuffles \n      × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions = 432 runs/task × 4 tasks = 1,728 total runs。\n    expected_results:\n      total_runs: 1728\n      tasks_completed: 4\n      # SST-2\n      sst2_seed_variance_pct: 8.4\n      sst2_lr_variance_pct: 42.3\n      sst2_data_shuffle_pct: 5.1\n      sst2_gpu_pct: 0.3\n      sst2_precision_pct: 0.1\n      sst2_seed_x_lr_pct: 12.7\n      sst2_residual_pct: 18.6\n      sst2_G_coefficient: 0.72\n      # RTE (small dataset, high variance expected)\n      rte_seed_variance_pct: 18.9\n      rte_lr_variance_pct: 31.2\n      rte_data_shuffle_pct: 11.3\n      rte_seed_x_lr_pct: 15.8\n      rte_residual_pct: 14.2\n      rte_G_coefficient: 0.48\n      # COPA (very small, extreme variance expected)\n      copa_seed_variance_pct: 22.1\n      copa_lr_variance_pct: 25.6\n      copa_data_shuffle_pct: 14.8\n      copa_seed_x_lr_pct: 11.2\n      copa_residual_pct: 16.8\n      copa_G_coefficient: 0.39\n      # Summary\n      variance_hierarchy: \"learning_rate > seed×lr > seed > data_shuffle > residual >> gpu ≈ precision\"\n      inference_vs_finetuning_diff: \"item → learning_rate as dominant source; precision remains negligible\"\n      bui_comparison_note: \"RTE seed variance 18.9% consistent with Bui et al. (2025) RTES finding\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Fine-tuning variance structure qualitatively different from inference：learning_rate取代item\n      成为dominant source（42% on SST-2），因为fine-tuning performance对lr选择的sensitivity\n      远大于对individual evaluation items的sensitivity。seed×lr interaction（12-16%）显示\n      training instability是lr-conditional的——特定lr+seed组合触发divergence。\n      \n      小数据集（RTE: 277 examples, COPA: 400 examples）的variance极大。RTE的seed=18.9%\n      与Bui et al. (2025)的RTES=18.22 for RoBERTa on COPA高度一致，提供cross-study validation。\n      COPA的G=0.39说明在这个scale上fine-tuning evaluation根本不reliable without averaging \n      across many seeds×lr combinations。\n      \n      Infrastructure facets（GPU, precision）在fine-tuning中也negligible（<0.5% combined），\n      与inference results一致——这是separability claim的bonus evidence，\n      虽然来自不同setting (encoder-only fine-tuning vs decoder inference)。\n      \n      Median档下exp-006的结果是interpretable但需要heavy qualification：\n      (1) encoder-only RoBERTa ≠ decoder LLMs；(2) task scale (SST-2: 67K) ≠ MMLU scale；\n      (3) fine-tuning variance structure根本不同于inference（不是\"same hierarchy, different magnitude\"\n      而是\"different hierarchy\"）。作为Discussion section observation而非numbered contribution足够。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S7: Fine-tuning Variance Decomposition (4 tasks)\"\n        description: >\n          4 tasks × 主要variance sources (lr, seed, data_shuffle, gpu, precision, \n          seed×lr, residual)。附G coefficient per task。\n          Highlight variance hierarchy inversion vs inference。\n      - name: \"Table S8: Bui et al. (2025) Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          Our RTE/COPA seed variance vs Bui et al.'s reported values。\n          Show consistency despite different experimental designs。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S7: Inference vs Fine-tuning variance decomposition stacked bars side-by-side。Left: inference (item_id dominant), Right: fine-tuning (lr dominant)。Visual contrast of different variance hierarchies。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-006在median档下cleanly delivers its downgraded role：Discussion-section observation\n      showing fine-tuning has qualitatively different variance structure。不需要是primary finding。\n      Bui et al. alignment是nice validation。Publication-worthy as supplementary evidence\n      但correctly scoped as encoder-only preliminary result。\n\n  - name: \"LayerCast precision mitigation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      LayerCast (FP16 storage + FP32 compute) as additional precision condition on MMLU。\n      量化这种precision mitigation的variance reduction效果。\n    expected_results:\n      layercast_accuracy: 0.6821\n      layercast_vs_bf16_delta_pp: 0.07\n      layercast_vs_fp16_delta_pp: 0.05\n      layercast_item_id_pct: 60.8\n      layercast_precision_effect_when_included_pct: 0.0003\n      layercast_precision_x_item_when_included_pct: 0.02\n      variance_reduction_vs_3precision: \"precision effects collapse to <0.001% when LayerCast replaces FP32\"\n      G_binary_with_layercast: 0.614\n      compute_overhead_vs_fp16_pct: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      LayerCast本质上是FP16+FP32的hybrid——storage in FP16, compute in FP32。\n      其accuracy与BF16/FP16几乎identical（Δ<0.1pp），因为BF16≈FP16已经established (D005)，\n      而FP32 anomaly是vLLM artifact不是genuine precision benefit。LayerCast therefore不提供\n      meaningful accuracy improvement over BF16/FP16，但也不hurt。\n      \n      当LayerCast替代FP32加入variance decomposition时，precision effects进一步collapse——\n      从already-small的0.0006% (BF16 vs FP16) 到trivial的0.0003%。这是because LayerCast \n      produces outputs nearly identical to FP16。Precision×item interaction也negligible。\n      \n      在median档下这个结果是clean但不exciting——\"precision mitigation works but isn't needed \n      because precision effects are already negligible after removing FP32 confound\"。\n      12% compute overhead for no meaningful benefit。\n      \n      Paper价值：作为completeness/practitioner guidance——\"if concerned about precision, \n      LayerCast adds 12% compute cost for no detectable reliability improvement over BF16\"。\n      One paragraph in Results or appendix。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S9: LayerCast Precision Comparison\"\n        description: >\n          4 precision conditions (FP32, BF16, FP16, LayerCast) × accuracy, item_id%, \n          precision effect %, compute time。Shows LayerCast clusters with BF16/FP16,\n          FP32 is the outlier。\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      exp-007在任何档位都不是paper的关键实验。Median档下它提供了一个clean practitioner takeaway\n      但不影响任何core claim。如果AAAI页数紧张，可以完全放appendix或甚至cut。\n\n  - name: \"MATH benchmark extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      MATH benchmark (200 items) — 测试reasoning-heavy tasks where chain-of-thought \n      introduces additional variance的item dominance pattern。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 230400\n      math_item_id_cross_model_pct: 30.2\n      math_model_x_item_pct: 35.8\n      math_prompt_x_item_pct: 9.4\n      math_seed_x_item_pct: 7.2\n      math_residual_pct: 11.1\n      math_G_item: 0.731\n      math_separability_binary_pct: 0.4\n      math_irt_gtheory_ratio: 3.3\n      math_d_study_G80_items: 620\n      cot_variance_contribution: \"absorbed into prompt×item and residual\"\n      math_vs_gsm8k_correlation: 0.82\n      accuracy_range_across_models: [0.21, 0.48]\n    result_rationale: >\n      MATH是最hard的benchmark（accuracy 21-48%），item_id进一步降到30.2%（vs GSM8K的32.5%）\n      因为extreme difficulty items的Bernoulli variance更compressed (p near 0 → p(1-p) small)，\n      同时model×item=35.8%因为models在hard math上disagree even more dramatically。\n      \n      Chain-of-thought不是G-theory的显式facet——它被absorbed into prompt×item (9.4%) 和 \n      residual (11.1%) 中。不同prompts elicit不同CoT strategies，导致prompt×item比\n      knowledge benchmarks高。但residual=11.1%反而比其他benchmarks低——因为MATH items\n      are more deterministic once you fix model+prompt+seed (either the model can solve it or not,\n      less random guessing than MC formats)。\n      \n      G_item=0.731是所有benchmarks中最低的，因为item difficulty rankings在models间最不一致\n      (model×item>item_id)——达到G≥0.80需要620 items，最多。\n      \n      MATH与GSM8K的item difficulty correlation=0.82说明两个math benchmarks的difficulty structure\n      有substantial overlap——\"math reasoning\"作为一个category有internal consistency。\n      这partial支持了gradient narrative（math benchmarks cluster together），但仍不够\n      claim monotonic cross-benchmark gradient。\n      \n      在median档下MATH加入后5-benchmark picture变为：\n      MMLU(42) > ARC(40) > GSM8K(33) > MATH(30) > HellaSwag(28)\n      看起来更gradual但ARC的位置仍然anomalous（knowledge-like benchmark在reasoning-like位置）。\n      而且HellaSwag最低不是因为\"hardest reasoning\"而是因为format-specific residual dominance。\n      Gradient story remains \"qualitative, not monotonic\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S10: MATH Variance Decomposition\"\n        description: >\n          MATH的full variance decomposition，与exp-002的3个benchmarks format一致。\n          Highlight model×item > item_id inversion（与GSM8K类似pattern）。\n      - name: \"Table 5 (updated): 5-benchmark Cross-benchmark Summary\"\n        description: >\n          扩展Table 5到5 benchmarks。排序by item_id descending。\n          附gradient non-monotonicity注释。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3 (updated): 5-benchmark stacked bars。MATH插入在GSM8K和HellaSwag之间。ARC仍然anomalous。\"\n      - \"Fig S8: Math-specific analysis — item difficulty distribution (bimodal: many items near p=0 and p=0.4) explaining compressed item_id variance。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-008作为P2实验在median档下adds marginal value。MATH的结果与GSM8K qualitatively similar\n      （model×item > item_id），strengthening the \"reasoning tasks have different variance structure\"\n      observation但不解决gradient non-monotonicity。如果timeline紧张（AAAI 9 weeks），\n      这是第一个cut candidate——GSM8K alone已经demonstrate了reasoning-task variance shift。\n      \n      如果included，MATH的主要added value是(1) 5th benchmark for cross-benchmark comparison,\n      (2) lowest G_item showing hardest benchmarks need most items, (3) CoT variance analysis\n      showing prompt×item absorbs reasoning strategy variation。这些是appendix material。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ecd9a1c2-6cfe-459e-a8ac-e63e308c50da","total_cost_usd":0.475406,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16422,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":14214,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16422,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":14214,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16422},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":11393,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.011488,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":14214,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16422,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.463918,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"87d57d63-3017-44a8-bfa8-150f09f7195f"}
